Z||000000||csmith3922||08-18-99||08:51 PM||||I recently purchased a 1988 fiero coupe for my daughter and the headlight doors suddenly stopped opening. they either won't open at all or the right sticks down and the left one just flaps. I remember hearing that this is common for this model but I don't remember the cause and correction. I would appreciate your help!
Z||000001||theogre||08-19-99||08:30 AM||||one or both motors may need work. These motors are controlled by a "brain box" that monitors the current the motors use and the system is pretty reliable.<p>The motors are generally easy to fix, as this version has shear pins that protect the gears. the pins are available from rodney dickman for about 5$ a side. It's time consuming but not dificult to tear them down.
